# Generate fresh COR04 keys per mutation; retain finalize keys with the current credential generation.
# operationKey = current Unix seconds + "." + UUID without hyphens.
# operationRecovery = base64 of 32 random bytes. New keys cannot reset durable deletion budgets.
@baseUrl = https://localhost:5001
@accessToken = replace-with-live-token
@operationKey = replace-with-fresh-key
@operationRecovery = replace-with-fresh-recovery-key
@idempotencyKey = replace-with-fresh-idempotency-key
@deleteApproval = replace-with-purpose-6-approval
@deleteToken = replace-with-published-email-token

### Fresh owner proof (eligible existing factor remains mandatory when configured)
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/reauthenticate
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Security-Operation-Key: {{operationKey}}
Security-Operation-Recovery-Key: {{operationRecovery}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"password":"replace-with-owner-password","purpose":6,"target":"delete:one-time"}

### Request with NEW operation keys and fresh approval; empty body selects one-time workflow
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/wipeout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Sensitive-Action-Token: {{deleteApproval}}
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}
Security-Operation-Key: {{operationKey}}
Security-Operation-Recovery-Key: {{operationRecovery}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Open the published mailbox link. GET is read-only and renders an encoded confirmation form.
GET {{baseUrl}}/account/wipeout/verify?payload={{deleteToken}}

### Explicit confirmation. Retain this form and its NEW keys for response-loss recovery/repeat submission.
# A browser submits the generated hidden fields. For this example supply fresh verification keys below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/wipeout/verify
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

deleteToken={{deleteToken}}&operationKey={{operationKey}}&operationRecovery={{operationRecovery}}

# Form values must be URL encoded (especially +, / and = in operationRecovery).
# Verification marks only this exact approved request; it never deletes the account.

### Deliberate authenticated completion with NEW operation keys; keep THESE keys for recovery
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/wipeout/finalize
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}
Security-Operation-Key: {{operationKey}}
Security-Operation-Recovery-Key: {{operationRecovery}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"deleteToken":"{{deleteToken}}"}

### Recovery does not require the deleted account's credentials
GET {{baseUrl}}/account/security-operations/status
Security-Operation-Key: {{operationKey}}
Security-Operation-Recovery-Key: {{operationRecovery}}

# For a newly chosen passphrase: approve target delete:passphrase and send the same
# passPhrase in request/finalize bodies. It never replaces fresh owner proof.
# Clear only the locally recorded credential generation when a committed step
# reports ACCOUNT_DELETE_SUCCEEDED. Admission-only/partial/pending outcomes do not mean deletion.
